# Local agent working notes
CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# Generated by jPipe from the .jd sources. The .jd files are the content,
# everything jPipe renders or emits from them is not.
*.svg
*.py
*.json

# ...except these, which are hand-written repository content, not jPipe output:
# the Codespace definition, and the chapter 2 example the models reason about.
!.devcontainer/devcontainer.json
!part_1/chapter_2/deployable.py
!part_1/chapter_2/deployable.json

# Chapter 4's execution layer is hand-written content: the bindings participants fill in,
# and the mocked artifacts the argument reads. The compiled shippable.json is kept too,
# even though it is compiler output, so that the CI job can run the argument without
# installing a compiler. 4.1 still has participants generate it, over the top of this one.
!part_2/chapter_4/exercises/*.py
!part_2/chapter_4/solutions/*.py
!part_2/chapter_4/mocks/measurements.json
!part_2/chapter_4/shippable.json

# Figures are drawn by hand, not rendered by jPipe. Everything under an images/ directory
# is kept, whatever its extension and wherever that directory sits.
!images/**
!**/images/**

# Python artefacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
build/
dist/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/

# macOS
.DS_Store
